<div class="wrap rows">
  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="when-title">
    <h2 id="when-title">When a windshield needs replacing</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>Your windshield is a safety part, not just a piece of glass. It helps hold the roof up in a rollover and gives the passenger airbag something to push against. Once it's badly cracked, it can't do that job the way it should.</p>
      <p>Replacement is usually the right call when:</p>
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>The crack is long</strong> or has spread well past the impact point.</li>
        <li><strong>The damage reaches the edge</strong> of the glass, where cracks tend to keep running.</li>
        <li><strong>It's right in front of the driver,</strong> where a repair could leave a blemish in your line of sight.</li>
        <li><strong>There are several chips or cracks,</strong> or a chip is bigger than a quarter.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not sure? Send us a photo. If a <a href="/windshield-repair/">windshield repair</a> will hold, we'll tell you, even though it's the smaller job.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <h2 id="how-title">How mobile windshield replacement works</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>Get a quote.</strong> Call or send your year, make, model, and VIN if you have it. The VIN tells us exactly which glass and camera setup your vehicle has.</li>
        <li><strong>We come to you.</strong> Your driveway or work parking lot anywhere in our <a href="/service-area/">service area</a>. All you need is room to open the doors.</li>
        <li><strong>Old glass out, new glass in.</strong> We remove the damaged windshield, prep the frame, and set the new glass in fresh urethane adhesive, with new moldings where needed.</li>
        <li><strong>Calibrate and verify.</strong> If your vehicle has a forward-facing camera, we recalibrate it on our own equipment and run a post-scan to confirm it's working.</li>
        <li><strong>Safe drive-away time.</strong> We'll tell you how long the adhesive needs before the vehicle is safe to drive. It's usually an hour or so, and we won't rush it.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/#quote">Get a windshield quote</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row row-dark" aria-labelledby="adas-title">
    <h2 id="adas-title">ADAS calibration in the same visit</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>Most newer vehicles have a camera at the top of the windshield that runs lane departure warning, automatic emergency braking, and adaptive cruise control. After a new windshield goes in, that camera usually has to be recalibrated so it aims exactly where the manufacturer intended.</p>
      <p>A lot of glass companies replace the windshield and send you to a dealership for the calibration. We do it in-house, in the same visit, so there's no second appointment. <a href="/services/#adas">More about ADAS calibration</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="who-title">
    <h2 id="who-title">Who does the work</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>Every replacement is done by {{ tech.name }}, a technician with {{ tech.years }} years in auto glass. Windshield replacement is his specialty. Every job is backed by our workmanship warranty, and we're insured. <a href="/about/#technician">Meet {{ tech.name }}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="before-title">
    <h2 id="before-title">Before we get there</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>Keep the crack clean and dry</strong> and avoid blasting the defroster or AC straight at the glass.</li>
        <li><strong>Clear the dash</strong> and anything hanging from the mirror.</li>
        <li><strong>Tell us about toll tags or dash cams</strong> stuck to the glass so we can plan around them.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
